//? Title: Golomb coding: split the quotient, fit the tail
//? Subtitle: Actual codeword spans, geometric expectations and checked bit-stream parsing
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
A stream of small nonnegative integers can waste space in fixed-width fields.
Golomb coding divides each value by a shared positive parameter, emits a unary
quotient, and appends a truncated-binary remainder. We begin with three
hand-checkable words, derive their lengths and the prefix property, and compare
parameters on an explicitly defined geometric source. Actual native records show
emitted and consumed boundaries; boundary controls distinguish clean exhaustion
from an incomplete word. The parameter and frame length remain external
information, and compression claims count logical bits rather than packed files
or runtime.
)

\toc

> Three words around the truncated-binary split

For \(M=3\), divide a value into \(n=3q+r\). Write \(q\) ones followed by a
zero. The remainder alphabet has three values: encode 0 as `0`, 1 as `10`, and 2
as `11`. The first gets a short one-bit code; the others need two bits. Values
6, 7 and 8 have the same quotient two, so their native records isolate this
remainder change.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/golomb_flow.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/golomb_analysis.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    const auto t = dm::algorithms::golomb_encode_trace({6, 7, 8}, 3, 3);
    const auto text = dm::algorithms::golomb_bit_string(t.bits);
    std::print("| n | q | r | unary | remainder | whole word | begin | end |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | --- | " "--- | --- | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (const auto &w : t.words)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", w.value,
                   w.quotient, w.remainder,
                   text.substr(w.begin, w.remainder_begin - w.begin),
                   text.substr(w.remainder_begin, w.end - w.remainder_begin),
                   text.substr(w.begin, w.end - w.begin), w.begin, w.end);
    const auto &w = t.words.back();
    dm::graphics::Diagram d(55, 1100);
    dm::graphics::DiagramNodeStyle box;
    box.width = 4.5;
    box.height = 1.8;
    box.font_size = 22;
    d.node("split", {0, 0},
           std::format("n = {}, M = 3\nq = {}, r = {}", w.value, w.quotient,
                       w.remainder), box).node("unary", {6, 2},
                                               std::format(
                                               "q ones, then zero\n{}",
                                               text.substr(
                                               w.begin,
                                               w.remainder_begin - w.begin)),
                                               box).node(
        "remainder", {6, -2},
        std::format("truncated binary r\n{}",
                    text.substr(w.remainder_begin, w.end - w.remainder_begin)),
        box).node("word", {12, 0},
                  std::format("concatenate\n{}",
                              text.substr(w.begin, w.end - w.begin)), box).edge(
        "split", "unary").edge("split", "remainder").edge("unary", "word").edge(
        "remainder", "word").text({6, 4},
                                  "One actual word: unary quotient + remainder",
                                  24).save_svg("build/golomb_flow.svg");
    if (text != "11001101011011")
        throw std::runtime_error("small dictionary");
}
```
