> Derive lengths and unique parsing

Let \(b=\lceil\log_2 M\rceil\) and \(c=2^b-M\). A full depth-\(b\) binary tree
has \(2^b\) leaves. Replacing \(c\) pairs of sibling leaves by their parents
leaves exactly \(M\) codewords: \(c\) words of length \(b-1\), and \(M-c\) words
of length \(b\). Assign the short words to remainders below \(c\); encode a
larger remainder as the \(b\)-bit representation of \(r+c\). The bit-length
formula is

$$q=\lfloor n/M\rfloor,\quad r=n\bmod M,\qquad
\ell_M(n)=q+1+\begin{cases}b-1,&r<c,\\b,&r\ge c.\end{cases}$$
\alttext(The length is the quotient plus its unary terminator plus either b minus one or b remainder bits, according to the cutoff.)

For \(M=1\), the remainder is always zero and has no bits, so the word is purely
unary. For a power of two, \(c=0\), and every remainder uses exactly \(b\) bits:
this is Rice coding.

The first zero uniquely ends the unary prefix. In the remainder, read \(b-1\)
bits; a value below \(c\) is complete, otherwise read one more bit and subtract
\(c\). These leaf codes are prefix-free, so concatenated complete words have a
unique parsing when \(M\) is known. Explicitly, their Kraft sum is

$$\sum_{n\ge0}2^{-\ell_M(n)}=
\left[\sum_{q\ge0}2^{-(q+1)}\right]
\left[c\,2^{-(b-1)}+(M-c)2^{-b}\right]=1.$$
\alttext(The unary quotient Kraft sum is one, and the short and long remainder leaves also use exactly one unit of binary tree capacity.)

The degenerate \(M=1\) remainder tree consists of the empty word, whose Kraft
sum is one; the displayed zero-coefficient short term then contributes zero.

> Retain the original length comparison

The scalar length API calculates logical size without constructing a potentially
enormous unary string. These are the original values 0,2,...,24 and parameters
2,4,8,16; the plot also includes intermediate values to reveal each integer
step. A small parameter saves remainder bits near zero but makes the quotient
expensive in the tail.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/golomb_lengths.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/golomb_analysis.hpp>
#include <datamunge/plot/diagram.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <limits>
#include <numeric>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    std::vector<std::uint64_t> original;
    for (unsigned n = 0; n <= 24; n += 2)
        original.push_back(n);
    std::print("{}\n",
               dm::algorithms::golomb_length_table(original, {2, 4, 8, 16}).select({"value", "M", "bits"}).to_md());
    std::vector<std::uint64_t> grid(25);
    std::iota(grid.begin(), grid.end(), 0);
    dm::algorithms::golomb_length_plot(grid, {2, 4, 8, 16}).save_svg(
        "build/golomb_lengths.svg");
}
```
